    <bpmn:process id="W_W4957" name="W4957. Over-Advance, Fraud &amp; Proceeds-Diversion Detection" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Continuous monitoring; certificate (W4939); field exam (W4943); anomaly alert
Frequency: Continuous + event-driven
Volume: Monthly monitoring across all 1–3 facilities/cycles
Owner: ABL &amp; Collateral Operations Manager / Internal Audit (VS-21) / Financial Crime (VS-86)
Participants: Finance (VS-17), Treasury (VS-18), Inventory (VS-05), AR (VS-16), Internal Audit (VS-21), Compliance (VS-86)
Source: workflow W4957 — Over-Advance, Fraud &amp; Proceeds-Diversion Detection</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4957_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4957_Lane1" name="Analytics">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4957_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4957_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4957_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4957_Lane2" name="Internal Audit">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4957_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4957_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4957_Start4" name="Continuous monitoring; certificate (W4939); field exam (W4943); anomaly alert">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4957_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4957_Task5" name="Detect over-advance: continuously test that availability (W4942) ≥ outstanding…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Detect over-advance: continuously test that availability (W4942) ≥ outstanding, that the certificate (W4939) excludes ineligibles (W4940/W4941), and that draws don&#x27;t exceed availability; alert on over-advance, certificate misstatement, or eligibility erosion
Responsible (R): Analytics / ABL Manager / Treasury
Accountable (A): Treasurer
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4957_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4957_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4957_Task6" name="Detect proceeds diversion (PD 115): monitor trust-receipt proceeds segregation…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Detect proceeds diversion (PD 115): monitor trust-receipt proceeds segregation (W4947) vs remittance (W4948), flag commingling/diversion patterns, reconcile trust-goods depletion to proceeds, and detect ghost sales/under-reporting (links VS-86 financial-crime)
Responsible (R): Analytics / Finance / ABL Manager / Compliance
Accountable (A): Treasurer / Compliance
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4957_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4957_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4957_Task7" name="Investigate &amp; escalate: investigate anomalies (data error vs fraud), escalate…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Investigate &amp; escalate: investigate anomalies (data error vs fraud), escalate confirmed issues to Internal Audit (VS-21)/Legal (VS-100)/the bank per the agreement, manage remediation and potential self-disclosure, and document for the audit trail
Responsible (R): Internal Audit / Legal / ABL Manager / Compliance
Accountable (A): CFO / Audit Committee
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4957_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4957_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4957_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4957_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4957_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-742 (ensure controlled execution — Collateral Release, Reconciliation, Compliance &amp; Analytics (PA-170.3).) | - CTL-742 (availability-first funding; proceeds segregated &amp; monitored; anomalies investigated &amp; escalated; audited (VS-21/VS-86))
Owner: ABL &amp; Collateral Operations Manager / Internal Audit (VS-21) / Financial Crime (VS-86)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
